Gut reaction first: these all feel like the same lecture with a gorier picture attached, and I'd probably barely look past the photo. A is the vaguest and just says "three overweight people", which is insulting to look at and tells me nothing I don't already know. The eye and the surgery pictures are grim, but I'd treat them as the sort of thing that's made to frighten people and then I'd get on with my biscuit. The bowel one is the most gruesome, and oddly the one I'd most want to look away from, though looking away isn't the same as changing what I eat.

Honestly, the diabetes one would bite most because I've got it, and a bleeding eye linked to the thing I'm already managing hits closer than cancer does. Still, I'd only give it a modest share. Nothing here tells me anything useful about how much sugar is in a bar, so none of them would really change my Thursday.

