Honestly, my gut reaction is that they all look like scare tactics aimed at someone who has time to care about bowel cancer on a Tuesday morning. The graphic photos would make me look away, and I'd probably just think "great, another lecture" and reach for the bar anyway, especially after a long day with the kids. The ones that mention a specific disease feel a bit more concrete, but I'd still be thinking about the price of the bar and whether I've got anything else to eat tonight. The plain "excess calories cause obesity" one with the photo of people from behind feels like it's judging people, which would just irritate me.

I'd give most of the points to the ones that name something I'd actually recognise from the NHS site or from my sister, and little to the rest. Realistically the labels won't do much to a chocolate bar I can get for under a pound.

