Honestly, my gut reaction is a shrug. Pictures of surgery and eyeballs just make me think of the telly, and I've seen enough of those in my life not to flinch. The "obesity" line on its own is the sort of thing I've heard my whole life, so it washes straight over me. I'd rather have a bit of a chocolate bar with my tea than look at a grisly photo, and I'm not going to be told off by a wrapper.

The one that might catch my eye a bit is the bowel cancer one, because my sister's husband had that and it made me think, though I'd still eat the bar if I fancied it.

