Honestly, my first reaction is that they're all the same leaflet with a different gory picture on it. The bleeding eye and the surgery shots make me wince, but I've seen worse on the telly and I just turn over. The ones with the people from behind feel like they're having a go at folk who look like me, and I'd switch off straight away.

I'm not going to be put off a bar of Dairy Milk by a warning on the wrapper. If I fancy one with a cup of tea, I'll have it. What would make me think twice is if it was about my own kind of problem, my blood sugar or my tablets, and came from somebody I'd trust like the pharmacist. The cancer ones are so broad they just wash over me, and "13 types of cancer" sounds like someone's trying to frighten me. The diabetes eye one is the closest to something I'd actually care about, but even that's a picture I'd rather not look at, so I'd probably look away and carry on.

